# Stage 1: example B1 with a mu- beam, everything P9-P14 owes inactivated,
# and Decay LEFT ACTIVE.
#
# One line more than mu+: `muMinusCaptureAtRest`. With it inactivated a stopped mu- has
# `G4Decay` as its only at-rest process and decays, which is what the port does in
# HadronicStage::kStage1. In the final configuration it is captured -
# G4HadronStoppingProcess::AtRestGetPhysicalInteractionLength returns 0.0 and pre-empts the
# decay outright (docs/RISK.md V38) - and the port refuses that by name.
# This row also carries the charge-odd dose split docs/RISK.md V44 records: the port's mu-
# was 3.78% high against Geant4 at stage 0 for reasons inside the EM ionisation chain, so
# read the difference between this row and muon_plus against that number and not against
# zero.
#
# THE _noelastic VARIANT. `hadElastic` is inactivated here as well, so this is the
# like-for-like for a port that has DECAY AND NOT ELASTIC. The difference between this
# file's dose and stage1_muon_minus.mac's is what hadElastic is worth for this species and
# this geometry - a measurement of the remaining gap rather than a claim about it.
# See stage1_README.md.
#
# Every name below is a row of ref/oracle/species_processes.csv for mu- - the dump of
# the constructed QBBC's own process manager. /process/inactivate ignores a name the
# species does not have, silently, so a macro written from the source rather than from
# the object can look like it switched something off. docs/RISK.md V43.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/process/inactivate muBrems
/process/inactivate muPairProd
/process/inactivate CoulombScat
/process/inactivate muonNuclear
/process/inactivate muMinusCaptureAtRest
/process/inactivate hadElastic

# The stage, recorded by what RAN and not by what was intended. docs/RISK.md V43's
# lesson: ask the object. This prints Active/InActive for every process on the
# particle's manager, after the inactivations above.
/particle/select mu-
/particle/process/dump

/gun/particle mu-
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn 500000
